// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Weak Certificate Mapping Enabled On Domain Controller
// Sigma ID: f823f0f0-3eba-4a4f-a414-e4bc24f5dbb5
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-10-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, credential-access, defense-impairment, T1556, T1649
// Description: Detects the Schannel "CertificateMappingMethods" value being set with the UPN mapping bit (0x4),
//   which allows implicit UPN-based certificate mapping for Schannel (e.g. LDAPS on Domain
//   Controllers) (ESC10). Attackers able to change the UPN of an account they control can then
//   obtain a certificate that authenticates as another principal. The KDC
//   "StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement" value is not covered: it is no longer supported since the
//   September 9, 2025 Windows update (KB5014754) and does not weaken Kerberos certificate mapping on
//   a patched Domain Controller.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators following the KB5014754 troubleshooting step that sets CertificateMappingMethods to 0x1F
// References:
//   - https://research.ifcr.dk/certipy-4-0-esc9-esc10-bloodhound-gui-new-authentication-and-request-methods-and-more-7237d88061f7
//   - https://github.com/ly4k/Certipy/wiki/06-%E2%80%90-Privilege-Escalation
//   - https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/topic/kb5014754-certificate-based-authentication-changes-on-windows-domain-controllers-ad2c23b0-15d8-4340-a468-4d4f3b188f16
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f669b19474f70bf0caf3142411b7509cf48c96b5/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dc_weak_certificate_mapping.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Schannel\\CertificateMappingMethods" and (RegistryValueData in~ ("DWORD (0x00000004)", "DWORD (0x00000005)", "DWORD (0x00000006)", "DWORD (0x00000007)", "DWORD (0x0000000c)", "DWORD (0x0000000d)", "DWORD (0x0000000e)", "DWORD (0x0000000f)", "DWORD (0x00000014)", "DWORD (0x00000015)", "DWORD (0x00000016)", "DWORD (0x00000017)", "DWORD (0x0000001c)", "DWORD (0x0000001d)", "DWORD (0x0000001e)", "DWORD (0x0000001f)"))
